# Disc-vis cache backups. The cache itself is ignored above, but ad-hoc copies
# made before risky runs are not covered by that pattern, and a 919 MB blob was
# swept into a commit that way (4a488b4). Match any variant.
data/disc_vis_cache.pkl*

# --- reproducibility carve-outs -------------------------------------------
# The blanket *.json and gfx/ rules above keep the working tree small, but they
# also leave a fresh clone unable to compile the paper or rebuild the claims
# registry. Re-include exactly the inputs those need. The gfx directory is
# un-ignored so git descends into it, then its contents are re-ignored and the
# five files paper.tex actually \input are named one by one -- the rest of
# paper/gfx/ is legacy artwork, and setpred/ also holds two generated figures the
# current paper does not use. paper/data/*.json (17 MB of per-polygon dumps) stays
# ignored on purpose: it is regenerable from results/ via build_paper_data.py.
!paper/gfx/
paper/gfx/*
!paper/gfx/fig_architecture.tex
!paper/gfx/setpred/
paper/gfx/setpred/*
!paper/gfx/setpred/fig_distributions.pdf
!paper/gfx/setpred/fig_mechanism.pdf
!paper/gfx/setpred/fig_operating_curve.pdf
!paper/gfx/setpred/fig_worked_example.pdf
!results/*.json
# build artifact of the Overleaf bundle, regenerated on demand
paper/agnet_overleaf.zip

# Peer-review correspondence: kept locally, never tracked. NOTE: these are still
# present in this branch's earlier history (27 commits) and were pushed, so
# untracking them here stops future exposure but does not undo the past one --
# that needs a history rewrite plus a force-push.
paper/reviews/
paper/response_to_reviewers.md
